WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:07.090 --> 00:00:10.210
This is the world's smallest country.

00:00:10.210 --> 00:00:13.640
The Vatican City State is less
than half a square kilometer

00:00:13.640 --> 00:00:17.040
in size and home to around 800 people,

00:00:17.040 --> 00:00:19.350
one of whom is the Pope.

00:00:19.350 --> 00:00:21.510
The Pontiff is not only the head of state,

00:00:21.510 --> 00:00:24.880
but is also head of the
government of the Catholic Church,

00:00:24.880 --> 00:00:27.030
known as the Holy See.

00:00:27.030 --> 00:00:29.740
This institution has
existed for the best part

00:00:29.740 --> 00:00:33.040
of two millennia, and
represents over one billion

00:00:33.040 --> 00:00:35.950
baptized Catholics worldwide.

00:00:35.950 --> 00:00:39.680
An old and secretive
entity, the Holy See acts as

00:00:39.680 --> 00:00:43.120
a surprisingly powerful
player in global diplomacy.

00:00:47.130 --> 00:00:49.720
This man shapes its foreign policy,

00:00:49.720 --> 00:00:51.250
Archbishop Paul Gallagher.

00:00:52.960 --> 00:00:54.750
Here are his key strategies

00:00:54.750 --> 00:00:58.010
on running the world's
oldest diplomatic service.

00:01:02.930 --> 00:01:05.180
The Holy See is determined

00:01:05.180 --> 00:01:08.380
and remains committed
to making a contribution

00:01:08.380 --> 00:01:12.180
to how things unfold in the
world and how relations unfold

00:01:12.180 --> 00:01:13.570
between states and people.

00:01:14.550 --> 00:01:17.980
The Holy See's ambassadors,
known as nuncios,

00:01:17.980 --> 00:01:21.170
represent the Pope in 183 countries,

00:01:21.170 --> 00:01:24.920
and have a permanent presence
at the United Nations.

00:01:24.920 --> 00:01:27.930
Here, the Pope and his
diplomats lobby other states

00:01:27.930 --> 00:01:30.950
to advance the Church's worldview.

00:01:30.950 --> 00:01:34.070
It argues against abortion
and contraception,

00:01:34.070 --> 00:01:36.550
but also promises peace.

00:01:36.550 --> 00:01:39.980
Nations and rulers
interacted with the Popes

00:01:39.980 --> 00:01:42.310
over the centuries, and that has continued

00:01:42.310 --> 00:01:46.610
to evolve and to change
up to our modern times.

00:01:47.550 --> 00:01:50.390
In Africa, papal envoys have mediated

00:01:50.390 --> 00:01:55.260
peace talks to end wars in
Sudan, Ivory Coast, and Burundi.

00:01:55.260 --> 00:01:58.180
But it can also be dangerous work.

00:01:58.180 --> 00:02:01.900
In 2003, the nuncio to
Burundi was assassinated

00:02:01.900 --> 00:02:05.300
by rogue rebel gunman, for
his part in negotiating

00:02:05.300 --> 00:02:09.070
a peace deal, ending the
country's decade-long civil war.

00:02:13.100 --> 00:02:15.150
Pope Francis comes with his own

00:02:15.150 --> 00:02:19.930
particular experience of
being a Latin American,

00:02:19.930 --> 00:02:21.910
being Argentinian, a pastor

00:02:21.910 --> 00:02:24.980
of a very big and important diocese.

00:02:24.980 --> 00:02:27.250
Pope Francis is the first non-European

00:02:27.250 --> 00:02:29.340
pontiff in modern times.

00:02:29.340 --> 00:02:32.240
He was at the center of one
of the biggest diplomatic

00:02:32.240 --> 00:02:35.800
coups of this century,
acting as an intermediary

00:02:35.800 --> 00:02:38.720
in talks between Cuba and America.

00:02:38.720 --> 00:02:40.950
These talks ended more than half a century

00:02:40.950 --> 00:02:44.470
of frozen relations
between the two countries.

00:02:44.470 --> 00:02:46.380
There has always been a tendency

00:02:46.380 --> 00:02:50.200
in the Church, to be
focused on particular areas,

00:02:50.200 --> 00:02:53.370
Eurocentrocism, North American-centrocism.

00:02:53.370 --> 00:02:55.140
I think what the Pope is
trying to say is that,

00:02:55.140 --> 00:02:58.880
"Let's have a global vision
for a globalized world".

00:03:03.410 --> 00:03:05.780
Today, more than 60 million people

00:03:05.780 --> 00:03:07.850
are displaced worldwide.

00:03:07.850 --> 00:03:10.550
Pope Francis has said that
this is one of the biggest

00:03:10.550 --> 00:03:13.680
global challenges of the 21st century.

00:03:26.330 --> 00:03:28.650
He believes it's a global problem,

00:03:28.650 --> 00:03:31.790
so it's something that
we've all got to shoulder.

00:03:32.790 --> 00:03:35.420
In 2013, Pope Francis called

00:03:35.420 --> 00:03:37.800
the mass drowning of
migrants off the coast

00:03:37.800 --> 00:03:40.990
of the Italian island
of Lampedusa shameful.

00:03:42.610 --> 00:03:47.560
15 days later, Italy launched
Operation Mare Nostrum,

00:03:47.560 --> 00:03:50.160
a naval mission to rescue migrants at sea.

00:03:51.140 --> 00:03:53.720
If we reject the refugee,

00:03:53.720 --> 00:03:58.310
we in some ways induce in
ourselves a certain indifference

00:03:58.310 --> 00:04:00.840
to the humanity of suffering around us.

00:04:01.720 --> 00:04:03.870
But the Catholic Church has been condemned

00:04:03.870 --> 00:04:06.793
for turning a blind eye to
decades of human suffering

00:04:06.793 --> 00:04:09.460
within its own institutions,

00:04:09.460 --> 00:04:13.040
a series of sexual abuse
scandals around the world.

00:04:13.040 --> 00:04:16.300
Pope Francis has pledged
to address these crimes,

00:04:16.300 --> 00:04:18.650
which have damaged the
Church's reputation.

00:04:28.350 --> 00:04:31.220
While there are calls to
modernize the Catholic Church

00:04:31.220 --> 00:04:34.010
and the way it's run, behind the scenes,

00:04:34.010 --> 00:04:37.720
the Vatican remains a powerful
force in global affairs.

